{"base_rate":0.3793584379358438,"brier":0.13357559274755926,"bss":0.4326690110707204,"bss_hi":0.5225270868287177,"bss_lo":0.32874591012497695,"country":"AT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08648535564853556,"ess":340.30634523682085,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Innsbruck</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Innsbruck rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 717 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nINNSBRUCK, 0.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 23 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(9&ndash;55) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>259</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>98</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>216</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Innsbruck</b> <span class=\"muted\">AT</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>9&ndash;55\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>717 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Innsbruck &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Innsbruck\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 88.34285714285714,330.0 195.04857142857145,200.0 308.86162162162157,86.86486486486484 403.9202777777778,19.68518518518522 403.9202777777778,33.16666666666663 308.86162162162157,160.64864864864865 195.04857142857145,283.2 88.34285714285714,370.85714285714283 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"243.91352859135287\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"243.91352859135287\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,374.97297297297297 88.34285714285714,318.8571428571429 195.04857142857145,220.8 308.86162162162157,155.72972972972974 403.9202777777778,90.46296296296293\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 259 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"374.97297297297297\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 98 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"88.34285714285714\" cy=\"318.8571428571429\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 39%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"195.04857142857145\" cy=\"220.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"308.86162162162157\" cy=\"155.72972972972974\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 216 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"403.9202777777778\" cy=\"90.46296296296293\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(38%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Innsbruck the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.52) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.34).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.345</td><td class='num'>11.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>161</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.351</td><td class='num'>9.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.443</td><td class='num'>6.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>196</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.519</td><td class='num'>5.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.26266,"lon":11.39454,"n":717,"n_cities":109,"name":"Innsbruck","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":259,"obs":0.019305019305019305,"sig":true},{"hi":0.23,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.0857142857142857,"n":98,"obs":0.17346938775510204,"sig":true},{"hi":0.58,"lo":0.23,"mean":0.3871428571428572,"n":70,"obs":0.44285714285714284,"sig":false},{"hi":0.85,"lo":0.58,"mean":0.7086486486486485,"n":74,"obs":0.6216216216216216,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.85,"mean":0.977175925925926,"n":216,"obs":0.8009259259259259,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":0.6,"rank":23,"rank_hi":55.0,"rank_lo":9.0,"reliability":0.011630120282309463,"resolution":0.11261277653858232,"slug":"innsbruck","station":"INNSBRUCK","timezone":"Europe/Vienna"}